# deps
# BOTH forms, deliberately. `node_modules/` (trailing slash) matches only a real DIRECTORY, so a
# `node_modules` SYMLINK — which is how a git worktree is usually wired to the main checkout's
# install — is NOT ignored by it. A bare `git add -A` in a worktree then commits the symlink, and CI
# dies at `bun install --frozen-lockfile` with `ENOENT: could not open the "node_modules" directory`,
# because the link points at a path that exists only on the developer's machine. Cost one red CI run.
node_modules/
node_modules
# builds — anchor to the actual adapter-node output dir. An unanchored `build/`
# also matched src/routes/build/ + src/lib/components/build/ (the core Build
# canvas), silently excluding the app's centerpiece from the repo + every deploy.
/frontend/build/
.svelte-kit/
dist/
# env
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# runtime scratch (per-run sandbox dirs, Session 3+)
.scratch/
# local verification evidence (screenshots/recordings from live drives) — not source
.evidence/
# logs / os
*.log
.DS_Store
.playwright-mcp/

# Local git worktrees used for parallel agent workstreams — never part of the tree.
# (They were briefly committed as embedded-repo gitlinks by a `git add -A`; this prevents a repeat.)
.worktrees/

# ⛔ EXCEPTION to the `*.log` rule above. These are TEST FIXTURES, not logs: captured CI output that
# backend/tests/ci-suite-guard.test.ts feeds to .github/scripts/assert-suite-ran.sh. Without this
# negation they are silently absent in a fresh clone and in CI, and the guard test fails there while
# passing on the machine that wrote them — a green-locally/red-in-CI trap with no visible cause.
!backend/tests/fixtures/ci-logs/*.log
